{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T01:25:23.401Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7a4af4b641f1e7f9180f8b98","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","claim:pm-gh1715","claim:pm-jbplbq","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-998juj+pm-gh1715+pm-jbplbq","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","claim:pm-gh1715","claim:pm-jbplbq","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T01:25:23.401Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-21T01:25:23.396Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Reader census (AC3), 2026-11-21. The shared decoder decodeHistorySnapshot (src/core/history/read.ts) feeds readHistorySnapshot, readIdentifiedHistorySnapshot and readHistoryEntries, which about 20 modules call: workspace-history, item-transaction, query/history, query/activity, query/get (claim state), ownership-source, history-read, governance/stale-work, governance/closure-timestamps, event-index, workspace-transaction, merge/receipts, lifecycle/restore, lifecycle/item-revision, lifecycle/checkpoint-rollback, history/maintenance (repair, redact, compact), governance/assurance and assurance-runtime, tombstone and runtime-primitives. All of them now get the typed refusal history_record_invalid (item_id, reason such as \"a JSON null\", details.line) instead of a reader dereferencing null.ts.\n\nReaders with their own line parser keep their behaviour. drift-scan (pm health / validate --check-history-drift) still counts the stream under unreadable_streams. storage-integrity still reports the line as unparseable. merge/three-way still refuses non-objects. history-storage-stats, provenance-health, health (tombstone classification, merge receipt references, telemetry state), author-attribution and merge/reconcile all skip or catch non-object values already. Salvage has its own decoder and now shares the decoder's predicate.\n\nScope decision: the decoder refuses only non-object values (null, boolean, number, string, array). A first draft also required string ts, author, op, before_hash, after_hash and an array patch on every object. It failed 26 specs because legacy streams and fixtures legitimately carry objects without author or without a patch array (one spec renders compact history for legacy entries with missing patch arrays). Objects keep each reader's existing tolerance.\n\nRecovery (AC2): history-repair --salvage-tail now removes a line whose JSON value is a null, a boolean or a number wherever it sits, since such a value cannot hold a record, and keeps every record byte-identical. The receipt gains non_record_lines. A string, array or incomplete object might encode a record, so salvage still refuses those. Executed in tests/integration/history-bridge.integration.spec.ts: a null line followed by a later pm write is salvaged, after which activity and health --strict-exit pass. Known limit: salvage still needs the retained records to verify, so a stream with both a scalar line and a chain break has no pm-native recovery (the decoder blocks the repair). Recovering that case means restoring the stream from version control."}]}],"before_hash":"41eca3dfd16f5b6eacc4ea63445040aaa2bc99450df5eddd04825d7fcb97a140","after_hash":"d26e035e747e195d3db1dcdb2c79cb77dc9e02149a2e9a797a1f5e7c01aac4b8","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"9e82dae3938bfdb9b36ae9ce156b78165e585e8627f8a7cf45fc3a81a2291400"}
